      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but how does that make its way back to the caller of getParameter()?\n\nThe \"value\" parameter is just a byte[] reference.  It\u0027s not a C++ pointer-to-an-array.  The new byte[vSize[0]] and subsequent assignment to \"value\" is a no-op that doesn\u0027t escape this method.\n\nThis CL just removes dead code as far as I can tell.  Can you double-check?",
